# WebSocket Rules

## Architecture Overview
```
Client Browser
    │
    │  WS /ws?token=<jwt>
    ▼
WsHub (Arc<Mutex<HashMap<BoardId, Vec<WsClient>>>>)
    │
    ├── Authenticates JWT on connect
    ├── Tracks which board each client has joined
    └── Broadcasts events to all clients on the same board
```

## Server — WsHub (`backend/src/ws/mod.rs`)

### Hub Structure
```rust
pub struct WsClient {
    pub user_id: String,
    pub board_id: Option<String>,
    pub sender: mpsc::UnboundedSender<Message>,
}

pub struct WsHub {
    clients: Mutex<HashMap<String, WsClient>>,  // client_id -> WsClient
}
```

### On Connect
1. Extract JWT from query param `?token=<jwt>`
2. Reject with 401 if invalid or expired
3. Register client in hub with no board yet
4. Start read loop (for JOIN_BOARD / LEAVE_BOARD events)
5. On disconnect: remove client, broadcast MEMBER_LEFT to their board

### Broadcast Rules
```rust
impl WsHub {
    // Send event to all clients on a board EXCEPT the sender
    pub fn broadcast_to_board(&self, board_id: &str, event: &WsEvent, exclude_client: Option<&str>)

    // Send event to a specific user (all their connections)
    pub fn send_to_user(&self, user_id: &str, event: &WsEvent)

    // Send to all clients on a board INCLUDING sender
    pub fn broadcast_to_board_all(&self, board_id: &str, event: &WsEvent)
}
```

### When to Broadcast
Every API handler that mutates board state must broadcast the corresponding WS event:
- `POST /api/lists/:boardId/cards` → broadcast `CARD_CREATED` to board
- `PATCH /api/cards/:id` → broadcast `CARD_UPDATED` to board
- `PATCH /api/cards/:id/move` → broadcast `CARD_MOVED` to board
- `DELETE /api/cards/:id` → broadcast `CARD_DELETED` to board
- `POST /api/boards/:boardId/lists` → broadcast `LIST_CREATED` to board
- `PATCH /api/lists/:id/position` → broadcast `LIST_REORDERED` to board
- `POST /api/notifications` → send `NOTIFICATION` to specific user

The API handler receives `State<AppState>` which includes `ws_hub` — use it directly.

## Event Format
All events serialized as JSON:
```rust
#[derive(Serialize)]
pub struct WsEvent {
    #[serde(rename = "type")]
    pub event_type: String,
    pub payload: serde_json::Value,
}
```

## Client — ws.ts

### Connection
```typescript
const WS_URL = `ws://${window.location.host}/ws?token=${getAccessToken()}`;
```
- Connect once on app load after login
- Store connection in a Svelte store so components can check status

### Reconnection
```typescript
const BACKOFF = [1000, 2000, 4000, 8000, 16000, 30000]; // ms
```
- On close: wait backoff[attempt] ms, reconnect
- On reconnect: re-fetch the current board's full state (don't trust cache)
- Reset backoff to 0 on successful open

### Token Refresh
- WS token is the short-lived JWT
- When JWT expires, WS connection will get a 401 close code
- On 401 close: refresh token, get new JWT, reconnect with new token

### Optimistic Updates
For drag-and-drop operations:
1. Update local store immediately (optimistic)
2. Send REST API call
3. If API succeeds: WS broadcast will come back (ignore it if state already matches)
4. If API fails: revert local store to previous state, show error toast

### Never Send Sensitive Data Over WS
- No passwords, tokens, or attachment content over WS
- WS is for state change notifications only
- Clients fetch full data via REST after receiving WS event if needed

## Heartbeat
- Server sends `{"type": "PING"}` every 30 seconds
- Client responds with `{"type": "PONG"}`
- If no PONG in 10s, server closes the connection
- Client detects close and reconnects
